      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "The Old Lodge, on Howth's favoured Thormanby Road is situated just above the village beside the entrance to Casana View, within a short walk of the Summit Inn. On a regular bus route with a dart service nearby, this location is incredibly convenient to all local amenities, while there are wonderful scenic walks within a few minutes stroll from home.\r\n \r\nNestled within a private secluded site this period “villa-style” home, is as delightful inside as it is from outside. The building features traditional painted rendered walls decorated by red-brick window and door arches along with red-brick corner quoins with pretty stacked chimney details above. The natural slate roof is neatly finished with led trimming and a discreet canopy detail beneath fixed guttering.  The pretty timber sash windows and split levels, surrounded by slightly elevated gardens create a unique aesthetic appeal that will be appreciated by all who view.\r\n \r\nA path leads from the cobble lock parking area to the front door. The entrance enjoys a sunny southerly aspect, hence the exterior dining table and chairs located here.\r\n \r\nOnce inside the main living space awaits, a cosy room featuring a wood burning stove surrounded by a stone mantel piece and warm herringbone polished timber flooring. The extra high ceilings are tapered and feature thick varnished timber beams while twin pairs of pretty sash windows complete with timber shutters complement this gorgeous room.\r\n \r\nBedrooms 3 & 4 are accessed on either side of the fireplace in the main living room. The front bedroom features a pair of ornate sash windows and a cast iron fireplace, while the inside bedroom looks into the private courtyard space to the rear and has a matching cast iron fireplace. Both rooms feature warm herringbone timber flooring.\r\n \r\nBeyond these three rooms is a central hall leading into the kitchen and dining space. There is a downstairs bathroom off the hall with a claw bath, a pull chain water closet and a whb. The floor is tiled and the walls are finished with painted timber panels.\r\n \r\nThere is a neat study with two velux roof lights at the rear of the hall. A door from the study leads to the private paved courtyard to the rear where morning coffee can be enjoyed in a sheltered space.\r\n \r\nThe kitchen comprises painted timber wall and floor mounted cabinetry, with integrated appliances, varnished timber and black granite worktops, a Belfast sink and a tiled floor. The dining area is open plan to the kitchen and at a slightly lower level with a varnished timber floor and well placed windows on three sides which frame views of green foliage visible outside. This is a particularly pleasant space to be.\r\n \r\nUpstairs off the landing is a second bathroom with a marble floor and tiled walls, a shower , wc, whb & heated towel rail. The main bedroom has varnished timber floors, four pretty windows and timber shutters, while the last of the four bedrooms is located beside this room and features a cast-iron fireplace, a separate walk-in wardrobe, a Velux window, and a hot press housing the boiler.\r\n \r\nOutside, gates open to a cobble lock drive with ample parking. The house is surrounded by an extensive lawn and mature planted boundaries. There are several areas to sit and relax in the garden that attract direct sunlight throughout the day. An elevated paved area at the top of the garden enjoys a pleasant aspect and there is a storage shed to accommodate ones bits and bobs !\r\n \r\nThe old Lodge needs to be viewed to fully appreciate its endearing charm and character. This is an adorable home, ready now for its very fortunate new owner.\r\n \r\nImperative viewing - by appointment only."
      },
